# Which top-level entries of the development tree a release exports.
#
# One entry per line: "public <name>" goes into the public release commit,
# "private <name>" never does. tools/release.sh refuses to prepare or export a
# tree with a top-level entry on neither list, so a new directory stays out of
# a release until someone classifies it here. tests/test_public_tree.py reads
# the private list from this file, and tests/test_release_tool.py checks that
# every tracked top-level entry is classified.
#
# The export reads this file as committed at the release tag.

public .github
public .gitignore
public .gitmodules
public CHANGELOG.md
public README.md
public THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
public VERSION
public assets
public bash
public bopos.config.example
public bopos.devices
public constraints.txt
public dashboard
public docs
public install-dashboard.sh
public install-device.sh
public patches
public pd
public python
public requirements-dev.txt
public run.sh
public systemd
public tests
public tools

# Development-only: work tracking, memory, records, arrivals, schedules,
# agent and editor settings, agent notes.
private .glean
private .loom
private .lore
private .nest
private .groundhog
private .claude
private .codex
private .obsidian
private .worktrees
private AGENTS.md
private CLAUDE.md
private inbox
